      "id": "claim_035a86dba6b44e0d9d871360d0b0a8c5",
      "statement": "`training/pretrain.py` owns the single-device training lifecycle: it loads YAML into `ModelConfig`, constructs and places `GPTOSS`, applies CUDA performance settings and optional compilation, performs an advisory memory check, creates AdamW and a warmup/cosine scheduler, loads packed-token batches, and performs mixed-precision forward, chunked cross-entropy plus auxiliary loss, backward, accumulation-boundary clipping and optimizer/scheduler steps, logging, interval saves, and final persistence.",
